     3	The Silver program's first road meet fell at the term's midpoint, at the river academy's own hall two days north — the confluence town, the season's best floor, the place a regional Iron title had been decided a year before — and the delegation went to it as a delegation for the first time since Norhold, because Withrow had ruled that Halcenvane's Silver entrant traveled under the academy's colors with the academy's people, proceedings or no proceedings, and the ruling had the whole of her tenure in it.
