   182	
   183	He had filed true reports on every one of them. That was the thing he had been proud of, once. In fifteen years he had never once put a false line in a return. A subject who did nothing got a report that said so. A subject who did something got a report that said exactly what, and no more. He had watched other monitors embroider, or guess, or round a dull week up into an interesting one for the sake of a better posting, and he had never done it. His product was the cleanest in the service. He had been told so. It was in a commendation, in a drawer somewhere.
   184	
