   183	And at the very bottom, in a different ink, in square capitals that had pressed so hard into the paper she could feel them from the back, the four words Rooke had copied onto it for her the night before, at the inn table, without being asked.
   184	
   185	She did not read them again. She had read them enough times last night, in the inn's narrow bed, with the bruise across her shoulders keeping her on her side. She knew exactly how they looked.
   186	
