   194	
   195	And the Silver in the corridor this morning, telling her to go on her fifth.
   196	
   197	That was the ladder. She could see every rung of it. Somebody had built it, and leaned it against the wall, and put her at the foot with her name on the first rung in a steward's hand, and every rung above it was there.
