+Seln's cutaway, and Chapter 27 still follows the refusal, aftermath, Anchor discussion, and closing
+in the source order. Chapters 21, 23, and 25 retain smaller clusters.
+
+Counting unit: one continuous manuscript passage following one source sentence, or one tightly
+unified source sentence-cluster, counts as one passage. When one source sentence becomes several
+manuscript sentences, it is one **split** passage. I did not count exact Tier A/B or packet wording,
+including *Prepare both roads*, *I'm not leaving the room while the text still works*, *It was the
